  "capabilityVocabularyFinding": "The contract probes agent-operation capabilities (read/publish/execute/status/cancel/resume/observe/review/store) while the registered lmstudio runtime advertises only inference operations (chat.completions, desktop.gui, embeddings, jit.model.ttl, model.lifecycle.by-key, openai.compat./v1, text.completions, vision.image_input). The two vocabularies do not intersect, so a model plan named `publish` was refused at the capability gate on real registry data. That is the honest end state of this round-trip, and the gap is recorded as ERR-138 instead of being papered over by loosening the check or by registering a capability nobody probed.",
